{"name":"Clay Slate Wacke","hex":"#cdcace","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"clay","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A mineral substance made up of small crystals of silica and alumina, that is ductile when moist; the material of pre-fired ceramics.","An earth material with ductile qualities."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To add clay to or to spread clay onto.","To purify using clay."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clay"},{"term":"slate","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A flake or piece of certain types of stone that tend to cleave into thin layers.\n A piece of such stone, usually cut into a rectangular shape, used as a tile for flooring, roofing, etc.;  such tiles collectively, or the material from which they are made.\n\nA piece of other material used as a roofing tile.","A piece of such stone, usually cut into a rectangular shape, used as a tile for flooring, roofing, etc.;  such tiles collectively, or the material from which they are made."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having the bluish-grey colour of slate (noun etymology 1, noun sense 4)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slate"},{"term":"wacke","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A soft, earthy, dark-coloured rock or clay derived from the alteration of basalt."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wacke"}],"entries":[{"title":"Clay","blocks":[{"text":"Clay is a type of fine-grained natural soil material containing clay minerals. Most pure clay minerals are white or light-coloured, but natural clays show a variety of colours from impurities, such as a reddish or brownish colour from small amounts of iron oxide."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/Boulder_clay_cliff_south_of_Withernsea_%28geograph_6054962%29.jpg/330px-Boulder_clay_cliff_south_of_Withernsea_%28geograph_6054962%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clay"},{"title":"Slate","blocks":[{"text":"Slate is a fine-grained, foliated, homogeneous, metamorphic rock derived from an original shale-type sedimentary rock composed of clay or volcanic ash through low-grade, regional metamorphism. It is the finest-grained foliated metamorphic rock. Foliation may not correspond to the original sedimentary layering, but instead is in planes perpendicular to the direction of metamorphic compression."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Slate_%28Knife_Lake_Formation%2C_metamorphism_at_2.7_Ga%2C_Neoarchean%3B_Rt._135_roadcut%2C_Gilbert%2C_Minnesota%2C_USA%29_3_%2823140002749%29.jpg/330px-Slate_%28Knife_Lake_Formation%2C_metamorphism_at_2.7_Ga%2C_Neoarchean%3B_Rt._135_roadcut%2C_Gilbert%2C_Minnesota%2C_USA%29_3_%2823140002749%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Slate"},{"title":"Greywacke","blocks":[{"text":"Greywacke or graywacke is a variety of sandstone generally characterized by its hardness, dark color, and poorly sorted angular grains of quartz, feldspar, and small rock fragments or sand-size lithic fragments set in a compact, clay-fine matrix. It is a texturally immature sedimentary rock generally found in Paleozoic strata. The larger grains can be sand- to gravel-sized, and matrix materials generally constitute more than 15 percent of the rock by volume."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Greywacke-f-and-l.jpg/330px-Greywacke-f-and-l.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greywacke"},{"title":"Slate gray","blocks":[{"text":"Slate gray is a moderate shade of gray with a slight azure tinge, which represents the average color of slate, a metamorphic rock often used in stonemasonry. As a tertiary color, slate is an equal mix of purple and green pigments."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/St_Fagans_Tannery_7.jpg/330px-St_Fagans_Tannery_7.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Slate_gray"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Clay_magnified.jpg/500px-Clay_magnified.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Clay_magnified.jpg/500px-Clay_magnified.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A 23,500 times magnified electron micrograph of smectite clay","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AClay_magnified.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Italian_and_African-American_Clay_Miners_in_Mine_Shaft.jpg/500px-Italian_and_African-American_Clay_Miners_in_Mine_Shaft.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Italian_and_African-American_Clay_Miners_in_Mine_Shaft.jpg/1280px-Italian_and_African-American_Clay_Miners_in_Mine_Shaft.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Italian_and_African-American_Clay_Miners_in_Mine_Shaft.jpg/500px-Italian_and_African-American_Clay_Miners_in_Mine_Shaft.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Italian and African-American clay miners in mine shaft, 1910","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AItalian_and_African-American_Clay_Miners_in_Mine_Shaft.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Clay_In_A_Construction_Site.jpg/500px-Clay_In_A_Construction_Site.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Clay_In_A_Construction_Site.jpg/1280px-Clay_In_A_Constructi